---
import CommunityLayout from '@/layouts/CommunityLayout.astro';
---

<CommunityLayout
  title="How We&rsquo;re Organized"
  subPage="how-were-organized"
  eyebrow="Distributed leadership + fiscal sponsorship"
  description="The people and structures that keep DT:FC running."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-8">

    <section>
      <h2>Distributed leadership</h2>
      <p>
        DT:FC is a not-for-profit business association, founded in 2022, that operates on
        distributed-leadership principles. There is no single artistic director or executive
        holding central authority. Instead, decisions are made by the people doing the work,
        coordinated through standing committees and a small Coordinating Council. Lacking a
        hierarchy encourages active membership and shared responsibility.
      </p>
      <p>
        Decision making is never a win/lose vote. When the membership reaches concordance, the
        decision is accepted as a new norm or behavior. When strongly opposing values emerge,
        the parties state their positions clearly, sit in reflective silence, and &mdash; if
        consensus still can&rsquo;t be reached &mdash; form a short-term committee to work out a
        solution together.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The Coordinating Council</h2>
      <p>
        The Coordinating Council (CC) consists of representatives from each standing committee.
        Current committees and their areas:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Competencies / Theatre Games</li>
        <li>Children&rsquo;s Theatre</li>
        <li>Shakespeare Track</li>
        <li>Workshops and Training</li>
        <li>Legacy (History + PhD Thesis project)</li>
        <li>Business Management (vision, values, website, marketing, funding)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Representatives rotate to the CC to keep decision-making in clear alignment with the
        organization&rsquo;s purpose and goals. For the purposes of the nonprofit registration,
        a Finance Committee member serves as Treasurer; a member is named President to call CC
        meetings, and another serves as Secretary to file meeting reports as minutes.
      </p>
      <p>
        The full membership may also gather for facilitated workshops, strategic planning, or
        any other need &mdash; with open-space agendas where participants bring topics and
        arrange them to fit the time available.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Standing committees</h2>
      <p>
        Standing committees own the ongoing work of DT:FC across all program areas. Short-term
        committees form around specific initiatives and dissolve when the work is done.
        Committees are open to any member who wants to contribute &mdash; that open access is
        what keeps the organization&rsquo;s leadership distributed rather than concentrated.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Fiscal sponsorship</h2>
      <p>
        DT:FC is fiscally sponsored by <strong>We Tell Stories, Inc.</strong>, a California
        501(c)(3) nonprofit with closely aligned goals and methods. Contributions made through
        <a href="/community/donate/" class="hover:text-teal-600">the Donate page</a>
        flow through We Tell Stories and are tax-deductible to the extent allowed by law.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</CommunityLayout>
